  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「アジョワン」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%A2%E3%82%B8%E3%83%A7%E3%83%AF%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 109904500,
      "text": "アジョワン（Ajwain、ajowan）またはTrachyspermum ammiは、セリ科の一年生草本である。葉と種子のような果実の両方が人間によって摂取される。英語の俗称「bishop's weed（司祭の草）」は他の植物も指す。「種子」（すなわち果実）はラベージの「種子」としばしば混同される。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Ajwain」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajwain",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1372081970,
      "text": "Ajwain or ajowan —also known as ajowan caraway, \nthymol seeds, bishop's weed, or carom—is an annual herb in the family Apiaceae. Both the leaves and the seed‑like fruit of the plant are consumed by humans. The name \"bishop's weed\" also is a common name for other plants. The \"seed\" is often confused with lovage seed."
    }
  },
